      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "CT has become the imaging modality of choice for diagnosing the specific cause of low back pain syndrome. This article describes and illustrates those abnormalities commonly associated with low back pain: disk herniation, spinal stenoses, facet joint abnormalities, spondylosis, inflammatory conditions of the lumbar spine, and sacroiliitis."},
